.TH ZEFF-BOY 6 "September 2026" "zeff-boy" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
zeff-boy \- multi-system video game console emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zeff-boy
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ rom ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zeff-boy
emulates Game Boy, Game Boy Color, Game Boy Advance, NES, ColecoVision,
PC Engine, WonderSwan, and Sega 8-bit systems.
Without a ROM argument it opens the graphical interface.  A supported ROM or
archive may be supplied on the command line to open it at startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--mode " auto|dmg|sgb|cgb
Select the Game Boy hardware mode.  The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.B --headless
Run without the graphical interface.  This option requires a ROM path.
.TP
.BI "--max-frames " count
Stop a headless run after the given number of frames.  The default is 600.
.TP
.BI "--load-state " file
Load a native save state at the start of a headless run.
.TP
.BI "--replay " file
Play a replay during a headless run.
.TP
.BI "--tas-verify " project
Verify a TAS project during a headless run.  Exactly one ROM path is required.
.TP
.BI "--tas-branch " id
Select the TAS branch to verify.  Requires
.BR --tas-verify .
.TP
.BI "--tas-export " file
Export the verified TAS branch as a replay.  Requires
.BR --tas-verify .
.TP
.B --apply-mods
Apply discovered ROM modifications during a headless run.
.TP
.B --no-apu
Disable audio processing during a headless run.
.TP
.B --no-sram
Disable battery-backed save RAM loading and writing during a headless run.
.TP
.BI "--screenshot " file
Write a screenshot from a headless run to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI "--screenshot-frame " frame
Select the frame captured by
.BR --screenshot .
.SH FILES
Settings, firmware, saves, screenshots, and other user data are managed from
the graphical interface and stored in platform-specific user data directories.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZEFF_MUTE_AUDIO=1
Disable host audio output while leaving emulated audio processing enabled.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/Zeffuro/zeff-boy/issues.
.SH AUTHOR
Zeffuro.
